ceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":656,"digest":"sha256:a1cf064d69b5dca046831a53b9f21abe7a853ebf9b37bf7547a81444d4d0d9c1","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-17T04:18:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T04:18:55Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1211-v0.12.11/m12stage11-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m1211-v0.12.11","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m1211-v0.12.11","body":"# Engacer OS M12.11 / 0.12.11 - Native multitasking\n\nM12-STAGE11-VM-v1 native qualification passes for these exact bytes. This is a scoped desktop delivery; complete public publication proof is tracked separately in the handbook.\n\nBuild: `72213fbfbc4e2bb33001b0a8b12ace54`.\nISO SHA256: `b94625c0f0870cd6df29ef6ee4f75e7c58f79e2ecd029acab1550a9b7e043373`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `c8fd4e476f352a2080d506f3e6ca46fd5ff8906d053a9f0b1d1015aa806f99f9`.\n\n## What changes\n\nAlt+Tab shows original icons and numbered document/folder identities, including\nminimized and unsaved state. Arrows, Tab and Shift+Tab choose within a bounded\nMRU snapshot. Alt release, Enter or the mouse commit; Escape preserves focus.\n\nThe window menu adds Arrange windows with previewed Left half, Right half,\nMaximize and Cancel choices. Supported half placement offers another actual\nwindow for the other side, or the choice to leave it unchanged. Existing edge\ndrag and Windows+arrows share this assistance. Each window restores its own\nnormal bounds. Compact unsupported halves are disabled with a useful reason.\n\nFile-dialog owners cannot be rearranged and are excluded from complementary\nchoices. Switching and arranging retain unsaved work. The eight-window quota\nand existing provider limits remain.\n\n## How and why\n\nReuse generation-scoped geometry and the existing eight-token array, adding an\nowner token and side value. There is no thumbnail framebuffer, extra process,\nworker or idle animation. Fixed shell state grows by 32 bytes to 552,957.\n[Design decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/66a044144479ddbf62147ad66a855f5498c22a4e/docs/architecture/multitasking-m1211.md),\n[window switching and layouts](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/66a044144479ddbf62147ad66a855f5498c22a4e/docs/handbook/multitasking-m1211.md) and\n[eight-step installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/66a044144479ddbf62147ad66a855f5498c22a4e/docs/handbook/install-m1211.md).\n\n## Verification\n\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/66a044144479ddbf62147ad66a855f5498c22a4e/evidence/M12/11/acceptance-results.json) binds\n591 compiled inputs and eleven native task/profile checks to actual native install/switch/arrange/drag/cancel, dirty\nwork, modal-owner protection, minimum refusal, quota and independent disk starts.\nCompact light/dark, actual 150% and physical 3840x2160/200% qualify the real\ncontrols. Enabled-device VMware, separate BIOS, twelve movement comparisons\nand real compressed boot repair pass for these exact bytes.\nThe actual C decoder passes 556 round-trip pages and 10,808 malformed/fuzz cases\nwith unchanged guard bytes and no heap allocation.\n\n[Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/66a044144479ddbf62147ad66a855f5498c22a4e/evidence/M12/11/resources.json) distinguish fixed, peak and\nretained pages; configured guest RAM is not measured OS consumption.\n\n## Scope and retained limits\n\n- Eight real windows; supported halves and maximize, no thumbnail caches,\n  arbitrary quarter layouts or virtual desktop expansion.\n- M12.14 retains shared-menu footer/conflict and Start query/notice feedback,\n  new-versus-saved Editor status and background transfer/file-dialog arbitration.\n  Finish/cancel transfers before opening a picker until that gate is qualified.\n- M12.16 retains cursor isolation and compact-startup versus explicit scale limits.\n- M12.18 retains the earlier concurrent BIOS/AHCI observation and complete final\n  controller/original-app matrix. Stress reliability is not established here.\n- Physical/ARM, vendor GPU 3D and universal Windows compatibility remain unqualified.\n- Agent review is not a human study. Public release and complete website proof\n  close separately before M12.12.\n\n![Actual native paired Files windows](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/66a044144479ddbf62147ad66a855f5498c22a4e/evidence/M12/11/feature.png)\n"}